# The PATHWAY - BONANZA's map between courses (wave 8R, SPEC.md 130.22).  The SHIPPED map since 2026-11-19:
# option A of docs/plans/bonanza-courses/pathway/ (the owner's concept sketch, "Faithful"), page 0 as the
# owner marked it up; PAGE 1 IS A PROTOTYPE ("screen 2 is fully undecided yet ... prototype only for now").
# The marble AUTO-ROLLS along a route between glowing pads: finishing course A by exit E opens the one route
# keyed (A, E), whose gate sinks; an arrow on that route's side of the screen takes it, Enter plays the pad's
# course.
#
#   page 1 (above, PROTOTYPE): 8 <-up-left- 7 <-up- 6        5 (up the right-hand climb from 4)
#   page 0 (below):            6 <-left- 3 -up-> 4
#                                        ^ up the right-hand road
#                              1 -right-> 2
#
# 1 FIRST ROLL (ROLL) and 2 LITTLE HOP (HOP) are the real first courses; 3 DOWNHILL DECISION is TRIAL standing
# in (its two exits the split) until it is built; 4 - 8 are the old test courses standing in.  The icons are
# docs/plans/bonanza-courses/pathway/gen.py's (32 x 24, placeholders for 3 - 8).  A screen direction is a
# ground step: +x down-right, -x up-left, +y down-left, -y up-right; both axes at once (equal amounts) down,
# up, left or right.
course PATH "The Pathway"
width  64
ball   rubber
pathway
music  fairway                              # (8b.10 gives the pathway its own)
rail   crystal                              # the route material (SPEC.md 130.22.8)
view   0 332                                # page 0's CGA window: 8 lines up, so the gate on 6's route and the
                                            # titles there are wholly on page 0 (the owner's mark-up)
pages  2
titles 5x7                                  # the map's titles in the 5 x 7 face (SPEC.md 130.22.2, 2026-11-19)
float  rect 0 0 64 64                       # the whole map FLOATS (the owner, 2026-11-16): crystal islands
                                            # with short icicle faces are the pathway's look (SPEC.md 130.27.2)

# pad N COURSE WX WY
pad 0 ROLL  21 28                           # 1 First Roll: where a new game rests
pad 1 HOP   24 25                           # 2 Little Hop
pad 2 TRIAL 24 17                           # 3 Downhill Decision (TRIAL stands in: two exits, the split)
pad 3 MILL  20 13                           # 4
pad 4 PEAK  12  5                           # 5 (page 1)
pad 5 MOON  15 17                           # 6
pad 6 PLAY   9 11                           # 7 (page 1)
pad 7 FIRST  4 11                           # 8 (page 1)

# route A B exit E [secret] [gate WX WY] path WX,WY[,H] ...
route 0 1 exit 0  path 21,28 24,25                  # 1 -> 2, right along the bottom road
route 1 2 exit 0  path 24,25 28,21 24,17            # 2 -> 3, right then up
route 2 3 exit 0  path 24,17 20,13                  # 3's exit 0 -> 4, UP (the Up arrow)
route 2 5 exit 1  path 24,17 15,17                  # 3's exit 1 -> 6, UP-LEFT (the Left arrow)
route 3 4 exit 0  path 20,13 12,5                   # 4 -> 5, up the right-hand climb into page 1
route 5 6 exit 0  gate 14 16  path 15,17 9,11       # 6 -> 7, up into page 1
route 6 7 exit 0  path 9,11 4,11                    # 7 -> 8, up-left

# icon N FILE SX SY [fps F] [title "TEXT"] [tdx DX]: frame 0 the rest pose, the rest while the marble rests
# here; a title on the map in place of the course's ("|" breaks a line), DX px off the icon's centre
icon 0 icons/first32x24.bba       -128 368
icon 1 icons/frog32x24.bba         -32 368
icon 2 icons/fork32x24.bba          56 352  title "Downhill|Decision"  tdx -25
icon 3 icons/mill32x24.bba          56 256  tdx -21
icon 4 icons/summit32x24.bba        24 128
icon 5 icons/moon32x24.bba         -80 256  tdx -26
icon 6 icons/playground32x24.bba    -8 160
icon 7 icons/trial32x24.bba        -88  96  title "Bounce Trial"

# the lives, one counter a page
lives 16 23
lives  6  4
